          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The concept of
            %em derived critical locus
            is the refinement of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/critical+locus"} critical locus
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+geometry"} derived geometry
          %p
            The formal duals to derived critical loci are described by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+formalism"} BV-BRST formalism
          %h2#details Details
          %p
            The following is a basic setup in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-geometry"} dg-geometry
            aimed at exhibiting the (formal dual of) the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complex"} BV-BRST complex
            as the derived critical locus of (the formal dual of) the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST+complex"} BRST complex
            (the example
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#ComparisonToBVBRSTExample"} below
          %h3#BasicDgGeometry Basic dg-geometry
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi dgcAlg
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgcAlg_k
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of unbounded cochain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded-commutative+algebras"} differential graded-commutative algebras
            (dgc-algebras) over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            An object in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ∈
